cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "greek-legacy-decode: recovering polytonic Greek from pre-Unicode font encodings"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Girardi
    given-names: Romain
    affiliation: "CEPAM UMR 7264, Université Côte d'Azur"
repository-code: "https://github.com/romain-girardi-eng/greek-legacy-decode"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - ancient-greek
  - polytonic-greek
  - digital-humanities
  - classics
  - patristics
  - legacy-fonts
  - unicode
  - pdf
  - text-extraction
abstract: >-
  Deterministic decoder for pre-Unicode Greek font encodings (Graeca, SPIonic,
  Bwgrkl, Odyssea, GrecMonotype, TimesGreek and others) as found in scholarly
  PDFs and documents typeset c. 1985-2005. Tables are derived empirically by
  aligning real documents against reference corpora and validated on held-out
  texts; unknown input is preserved and flagged, never guessed.
